{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `obs_times`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target += log_survival(obs_times[n], gamma) + log_hazard(obs_times[n], gamma)` loop with the equivalent built-in vectorized sampling statement `obs_times ~ exponential(gamma)`. This preserves the same log density for nonnegative observation times because the original contribution is `log(gamma) - gamma * obs_times[n]`. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  // Survival function
  real log_survival(real t, real gamma) {
    return -gamma * t;
  }

  // Inverse survival function
  real inv_survival(real u, real gamma) {
    return - log(u) / gamma;
  }
}

data {
  int<lower=1> N;             // Number of observations
  array[N] real<lower=0> obs_times; // Observation times

  int<lower=1> N_display;                 // Number of display times
  array[N_display] real<lower=0> display_times; // Display times
}

parameters {
  real<lower=0> gamma;
}

model {
  gamma ~ normal(0, 5);
  obs_times ~ exponential(gamma);
}

generated quantities {
  array[N_display] real display_survival;
  array[N] real<lower=0> pred_obs_times;

  for (n in 1:N_display)
    display_survival[n] = exp(log_survival(display_times[n], gamma));

  for (n in 1:N)
    pred_obs_times[n] = inv_survival(uniform_rng(0, 1), gamma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"N_display":2,"display_times":[1.0,2.0],"obs_times":[1.0,2.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["obs_times"]}
